                "value": [
                  "Pennsylvania",
                  "Maryland"
                ],
                "exact_quote": "EHR data were encoded using standard healthcare terminologies and then combined using the PCORnet-specified Common Data Model (CDM). The PCORnet CDM transforms each healthcare system's dialect into a common language standardized on the meaningful use-recommended vocabularies (SNOMED, RxNORM, and LOINC). In this study, our analysis included adult patients (18 years or older) with their first COVID-19 diagnosis between 1 March 2020 and 28 February 2021.",
                "page_number": 2
              },
              "countries": {
                "value": [
                  "United States"
                ],
